<configuration name="local_stream.conf" description="stream json config">
  <!--
      S2-20 (G-47, docs/decisions.md): same bug class G-50/G-47 already
      found and fixed for `mod_conference`/`mod_callcenter` — confirmed
      live, `mod_local_stream` fails to *load at all* without this file
      (`mod_local_stream.c:1337 Open of local_stream.conf failed`, then
      `Error Loading module .../mod_local_stream.so`). Without the module
      loaded, `local_stream://moh` (`buildCallcenterConfigurationDocument`'s
      own default `moh-sound` when a queue has no uploaded MOH asset) isn't
      merely silent — it's an *unrecognized file format entirely*, and
      confirmed live this doesn't fail once and move on: `mod_callcenter`
      retried opening it in a tight loop (`switch_core_file.c:346 Invalid
      file format [local_stream] for [moh]!`, thousands of times a second)
      for the *entire* time a caller sat in queue, never actually reaching
      the point of ringing an agent — a hard hang, not a cosmetic MOH gap.

      `path` points at an empty directory (no sound files ship in this
      image at all — see the Dockerfile's own comment on
      files.freeswitch.org requiring auth): confirmed live this is fine.
      `mod_local_stream` treats a directory with zero files as an
      indefinite comfort-noise/silence generator, not a load error — the
      same "degrades to silence, not to a hang or a crash" shape this
      image's other MOH/prompt gaps already establish (`valet_hold_music`,
      G-48; the PIN prompts, G-50).
  -->
  <directory name="moh" path="/usr/share/freeswitch/sounds/moh" rate="8000" shuffle="false" timer-name="soft"/>
</configuration>
